Column $C$ contains only dashes, so $C$ is the source. Row $A$ contains only dashes, so $A$ is the sink.
Read each capacity from its starting row to its ending column: $C\to B$ has capacity $7$, $C\to D$ has capacity $11$, $B\to A$ has capacity $9$ and $D\to A$ has capacity $8$.
Place $C$ at the left and $A$ at the right. Label the edges with capacities in kL/h.
[tikz]\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\usetikzlibrary{decorations.markings}
\tikzset{midarrow/.style={decoration={markings,mark=at position 0.55 with {\arrow{>}}},postaction={decorate}}}
\coordinate (C) at (0,1.4);\coordinate (B) at (2.4,2.8);\coordinate (D) at (2.4,0);\coordinate (A) at (4.8,1.4);
\draw[midarrow] (C)--(B) node[pos=0.35,above left] {$7$};
\draw[midarrow] (C)--(D) node[pos=0.35,below left] {$11$};
\draw[midarrow] (B)--(A) node[pos=0.35,above right] {$9$};
\draw[midarrow] (D)--(A) node[pos=0.35,below right] {$8$};
\fill[black] (C) circle (2pt) node[left] {$C$};
\fill[black] (B) circle (2pt) node[above] {$B$};
\fill[black] (D) circle (2pt) node[below] {$D$};
\fill[black] (A) circle (2pt) node[right] {$A$};
\end{tikzpicture}[/tikz]

